AI peace: Player.PeacePriceFor(gameData, other) is the gold an AI wants for peace (0 = free, int.MaxValue = refused: refuse-contact window, locked war, war under 10 turns old, longer after a broken treaty) and grows with its lead in the war, fading as the war drags on; WouldAcceptDealFrom accepts a partOfPeaceTreaty offer only at war and at that price; AIs sign peace with each other through ExecuteDeal (the loser paying the winner's price) and offer a human peace every 5 turns when their price is 0 (MsgShowTradeOffer, both sides flagged partOfPeaceTreaty); a war declared within 50 turns of a peace treaty is remembered (PlayerRelationship, saved with the game) and the AI keeps its own treaties that long.

